  "captureStorage": "Raw captures and browser receipts retained as ignored private evidence; no private capture paths linked from maintained documentation",
  "findings": [
    "Component figure: schema-10 request-intent/routing Registry, Native options/admission/sessions and filesystem/models/controls boundaries, local approvals/credentials/legacy pins, outbound WSS and evidence/profile routes are readable in both themes at both reviewed HTML sizes. No label clipping or route-through-node collision observed in those figure areas.",
    "Workflow figure: the scope-browsing/selection row, immutable dispatch-or-successor preparation, Native execution authority, saved-guard passive resolution, compact inventory binding/receipt/refusal and conditional present/uncertain branch are readable in both themes at both reviewed HTML sizes.",
    "Workflow initial HTML view leaves the final CLI ownership row at the viewport edge, where the fixed navigation dock obscures part of it. Scrolling 420px exposes the complete lower row and legend in both themes at 1440x900.",
    "Standalone canonical Auto SVG figures show all component nodes and all six workflow rows/routes without the HTML navigation dock in both emulated themes at 1600x1200.",
    "The changed visible labels preserve the separate Gateway, local-profile and Native owners. This is perceptual review of communication artifacts, not evidence that the described Native or Gateway runtime behavior passed acceptance."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Workflow HTML requires vertical page scrolling; the complete figure is not claimed to be unobscured in one initial viewport.",
    "Supporting cards were visible only in part at the bottoms of some HTML captures and were not fully reviewed. The interactive source explorer was not visually inspected.",
    "Perceptual judgment covers only the 14 listed images, Chrome and the recorded sizes/themes; no accessibility audit or other-browser/screen/platform proof is claimed.",
    "Standalone SVG omits the HTML title, supporting cards and source explorer. Preserve HTML/JSON alongside SVG to retain candidate status and source/contract limits.",
    "No Gateway runtime, Native implementation, installed-provider continuation, physical-device/network, Cloud-client, seven-day usability or release acceptance is established by diagram checks or this visual review."
  ],
